#4471 merged every date report into one known parser bug. The reports are two
causes. Cause follows the tenant (locale and booking form), not the subject
line and not intake's tag.

<Callout kind="warn">
#4471 is not one issue. The hint reports have no ticket of their own.
</Callout>

## What was merged

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## parser

The shared parser reads every date month first. A day-first tenant's dates come
out flipped: 7 April becomes 4 July. App, email, and booking-v2 forms all hit
this. That is the bulk of #4471.

## hint

booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under the date field. People type what the hint
says. The form still reads the date the tenant's way (day first). The month
flips for a different reason. Same subject as parser; not the same bug.

## Why they sat in one ticket

Triage merges on subject ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)).
Intake tags from the browser locale, which often disagrees with the tenant.
Neither is the cause. Split #4471: one ticket per cause, with the report count
from the table.

## 5 October

Engineering closed #4471.

- `parser` — FIXED — `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`
- `hint` — WON'T FIX — booking-v3 form retired

